      <string id="PREF_AboutDialog">'About Foxit PDF Editor' Dialog</string>

	<string id="PREF_templates">Configure templates for watermark, background, header/footer, and stamp</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_watermark">Configure a shared path for watermark templates storing:</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_Allow1">Do not allow users to use templates created by themselves</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_Allow2">Do not allow users to use templates created by themselves</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_Allow3">Do not allow users to use templates created by themselves</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_Allow4">Do not allow users to use templates created by themselves</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_background">Configure a shared path for background templates storing:</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_headerfooter">Configure a shared path for header/footer templates storing:</string>
	<string id="PREF_templates_stamp">Configure a shared path for stamp templates storing:</string>
        <string id="PREF_templates_Explain">Choose "Enabled" to allow users to configure shared templates for watermark, background, header&amp;footer, and stamp.

Configure a shared path for templates storing:
Enter or select a shared path to store the template. The templates will be read in this path when the user uses the watermark,background, header/footer, or stamp functions in Foxit PDF Editor.
Please note that the template file format needs to be the same as the template format created in Foxit PDF Editor. Please ensure that you provide the correct template path, otherwise, you may encounter an error when trying to read the template. For example, the path you fill in the watermark module will only be used to read the watermark template.

Do not allow users to use templates created by themselves:
Uncheck this option, users will be allowed to use the templates that created by themselves. 
Check this option, users will not be allowed to use the templates that created by themselves.

This will change the setting of templates in Comment>Stamp or Organize>Watermark/Background/header&amp;footer.</string>
      <string id="PREF_Advertise">Advertisement</string>
      <string id="PREF_AdvertiseFolderPath">Folder Path:</string>
      <string id="Advertise_Explain">Enable this option to change the settings of advertisement in right corner of the tab bar.
	  
Check 'Remove Advertisement' to hide advertisements in the right corner of the tab bar and disable the setting in 'Preferences > General > Application Startup'.</string>

      <string id="PREF_Application_Language_Explain">Enable this option to change the application language settings.

Check 'Don't Show Community Languages' to hide community languages.Otherwise community-translated languages will be listed under official languages.

Default Application Language: Input a language file name, such as 'lang_en-us.xml', to set this language as default application language. This will remove the setting item in 'Preferences > Languages'.</string>
      <string id="PREF_ApplicationLanguage">Application Language</string>
      <string id="PREF_AutoHideStatusBar">Auto-hide Status Bar</string>
	  <string id="PREF_OnlydisplaySign">Only display the Sign In page for users (available for Subscription Release)</string>
	  <string id="PREF_OnlydisplaySign_Explain">Enable this option to only display the Sign In page when launching Foxit PDF Editor.
	   
Note: this option is only available for Foxit PDF Editor Subscription Release.</string>
	   
	  <string id="PREF_Donotallowaccount_Explain">Enable this option to not allow new account creation.
	  
The 'Create a new account' option will not appear in the login page and not allow users to sign up a Foxit account in Foxit PDF Editor.</string>
	  <string id="PREF_Donotallowaccount">Do not allow new account creation</string>
     <string id="PREF_Requestforactivation_checkbox">select how to activate product:</string>
      <string id="PREF_Requestforactivation_checkbox3">Display both of the above methods</string>
      <string id="PREF_Requestforactivation_checkbox2">Only display the Sign In page for users</string>
      <string id="PREF_Requestforactivation_checkbox1">Only display the registration code input box for users</string>
	  <string id="PREF_Requestforactivation">Request for activation when launching the application (available for Perpetual Release)</string>
	  <string id="PREF_Requestforactivation_Explain">Enable this option to request for activation when launching the application. 

This will skip the startup page and go to the activation dialog directly. And there are 3 options to select how to activate product:
Only display the registration code input box for users: select this option will only support to activate by registration code input.
Only display the Sign In page for users: select this option will only support to activate by signing with AC account.
Display both of the above methods: select this option will support to activate by registration code input or signing in with AC account.

Note: this option is only available for Foxit PDF Editor Perpetual Release</string>
      <string id="PREF_Selectloginmethods_Explain">Enable this option to hide some login methods in user interface.

The selected login methods will be hidden in the user login interface.</string>
	  <string id="PREF_Selectloginmethods">Hide the unnecessary login methods in the login page</string>
	  <string id="PREF_Disableloginmethods">Hide the unnecessary login methods in the login page</string>
