	<string id="PREF_AddPrivilegedLocations_Explain">Enable this option to disable and lock the end user's ability to add files, folders, and hosts as a privileged location prevents them from assigning trust and thereby exempting that location from enhanced security restrictions.
Input the file path, folder path or host name which need to be added to the privileged location list.</string>

<string id="PREF_SecurityConfig">Security Settings</string>
<string id="PREF_PDFAction_Checkbox">Disable PDF redirection actions</string>
<string id="PREF_PDFAction">Disable all actions in PDFs</string>
<string id="PREF_PDFAction_Explain">Enable this option to disable all actions in PDFs. The application will block all actions in PDF files, including GoToE, GoToR, Launch, Thread, Import Data, Submit Form, and Reset Form.</string>
<string id="PREF_Attachments">All file attachments may be opened or saved to disk</string>
<string id="PREF_Attachments_Explain">This setting specifies the default permission settings of opening/saving non-PDF files.

Enable this option to allow all file attachments to be opened or saved to disk.

Disable this option to forbid file attachments to be opened or saved to disk.

If the item is enabled, the application will allow opening/saving any file type other than PDF. To check this in the product, go to Trust Manager and verify the PDF File Attachments options in Preferences are available.</string>
<string id="PREF_Editdefault_emy"></string>
<string id="PREF_Editdefault_Example">Example: version:1|.ade:3|.adp:3|.app:3|.arc:3|.arj:3|</string>
<string id="PREF_Editdefault">Edit the default list of file types (Extension)</string>
<string id="PREF_Editdefault_Explain">In the "Edit the default list of file types (Extension)" list, you can set a whitelist and blacklist of file types other than PDF to control which file types are allowed to be opened from a document.
Please note that in case of duplicate entries, the product will only consider the value of the first entry.
Every item in the list should include an extension and a numerical value indicating the permission level:
0: Users are alerted to potential file safety risks and given two choices: open the file, permanently allow access.
1: Users are alerted to potential file safety risks and given three choices: open the file, permanently allow access, or permanently restrict access.
2: Always open this file type.
3: The file type is restricted from being opened as an attachment, launching it is also not allowed, and a window message is displayed.</string>

	<string id="PREF_UpdateConfig">Update Settings</string>
	<string id="PREF_UpdateConfig_Explain">Settings for update features.</string>
	<string id="PREF_ActivationSettings">Activation Settings</string>
	<string id="PREF_ActivationSettings_Explain">Settings for Activation features.</string>
    <string id="PREF_DisableMajorUpdate">Disable major updates, but still show minor/maintenance updates</string>
    <string id="PREF_DisableMajorUpdate_Explain">Enable this option to show you only minor/maintenance updates.

Disable this option to show you all updates (major updates, minor updates and maintenance updates).</string>
    <string id="PREF_ModifyActivationServer">Modify the address of the Activation server</string>
    <string id="PREF_ModifyActivationServerUrl">Activation server address:</string>
    <string id="PREF_ModifyActivationServer_Explain">Enable this option to define the Activation server address for Foxit PDF Editor, so that it will use this address for Activation or Deactivation.</string>
    <string id="NULL_Explain"></string>
    <string id="DisableActionOpenFile_Explain">This setting determines whether the application is allowed to open/execute non-PDF files.

Disable all actions to open/execute non-PDF files: When the item is selected, the application is not allowed to perform all actions of opening/executing non-PDF files.

Disable the action to open/execute the specified non-PDF file types: When the item is selected, the application is allowed to open/execute non-PDF files, except for those specified in the non-PDF file type lists.</string>
     <string id="DisableActionsOpenFileAll">Disable all actions to open/execute non-PDF files</string>
     <string id="DisableActionsOpenFileOption">Action to open/execute non-PDF files</string>
     <string id="DisableActionsOpenFilePart">Disable the action to open/execute the specified non-PDF file types</string>      
     <string id="RMS_DKE">Enable Double Key Encryption (DKE)</string>
     <string id="RMS_DKE_Explain">Enable this option to allow authenticated domain users to access Double Key Encryption (DKE) services. Please ensure that the required permissions and configurations are correctly set up in Microsoft Purview and Azure Key Vault for seamless operation.</string>
  </stringTable>
